      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:description": "FERA discount applied to PG&E residential base plans E-1, E-TOU-C, E-TOU-D, EV2 and E-ELEC. Sheet 1: \"Customers taking service on this rate schedule will receive an 18 percent discount on their total bundled volumetric charges on their otherwise applicable rate schedule\", and \"Discounts will be applied as a residual reduction to distribution charges, after FERA customers are exempted from the Wildfire Hardening Charge, Recovery Bond Charge, and the Recovery Bond Credit.\" Those exemptions are carried as urpx:multiplier -1 over the composed base's own charge, and the discount as urpx:multiplier -0.18 over the base's FERA-discountable urpx:PriceSummary, which includes the generation charges; each names its candidates in all five base plans, read as alternatives. The base services charge is not discounted: Sheet 1 assigns a FERA customer to Income Tier 2, which each base prices as a urpx:ProfileAlternative.",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-06-01T00:00:00",
      "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
      "urpx:commodity": {
        "@id": "urpx:electricity"
      },
