      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "pge:cc-e-fera-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "pge:cc-e-fera-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 6 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) The discount took effect before this version. Sheet 1, which states it, has been effective since March 1, 2026, and this version is dated June 1, 2026 by Sheet 2's income table; the corpus holds no E-FERA version for March 1 through May 31, 2026. (2) The 50 percent discount \"on the delivery minimum bill amount, if applicable\" has nothing to apply to: none of the five bases carries a delivery minimum bill. Each prices a base services charge instead, and Sheet 1 assigns a FERA customer to Income Tier 2 of it. (3) Nothing selects Income Tier 2. Sheet 1: \"Customers enrolled on E-FERA are assigned to Income Tier 2 for a base services charge if their otherwise applicable rate includes a base services charge.\" The base services charge is a urpx:ProfileAlternative on each base (on pge:e-1 it is in the sibling pge:e-1-income-tier modifier, which a composition with this modifier does not include), and nothing in URPX ties a modifier to an alternative, so a scenario cost model can pair this modifier with the Income Tier 1 or Tier 3 base services charge. (4) The master-meter provision is not modeled: Sheet 1 takes the FERA discount on the total non-CARE portion of bundled charges, multiplied by the number of FERA units divided by the number of non-CARE units, for customers served under Schedules ES, ESL, ESR, ESRL, ET or ETL, none of which this corpus holds. (5) Direct access and community choice aggregation customers are not modeled. Sheet 1: \"The FERA discount will be calculated for direct access and community choice aggregation customers based on the total charges as if they were subject to bundled service rates.\" This version declares bundled service, and a departed customer's composition would need both this modifier and the base's vintage-PCIA modifier. (6) Eligibility is carried as residential customer kind and enrollment in pge:program-fera. The Sheet 1 and Sheet 2 income criteria (200 percent plus $1 to 250 percent of federal poverty guidelines, $43,281 to $54,100 for one or two persons through $111,441 to $139,300 for eight, plus $11,360 to $14,200 per additional person), the three-or-more-persons requirement, the Special Condition 2 limit to the primary residence, the exclusion of CARE participants, of master-metered customers without sub-metering on Schedule EM or EM TOU and of Schedule E-CARE customers are not data.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-05T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
